.TH LSP 1
.SH NAME
lsp \- ask lspfs a question
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lsp
.I kind
[
.I arg ...
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Lsp
asks
.IR lspfs (4),
mounted on
.BR /mnt/lsp ,
the question
.I kind
names, and prints the answer.
It opens
.BI /mnt/lsp/ kind
for reading and writing, writes its
.IR arg s,
joined by blanks, and copies what it reads to standard output.
The kinds and what each takes are those of
.IR lspfs (4):
.B def
and
.B refs
take a place,
.B wsyms
a file or directory and a query, and
.B diags
a file or directory.
.SH EXAMPLES
The functions and types whose names match
.B fo
in the project under the current directory:
.IP
.EX
lsp wsyms `{pwd} fo
.EE
.PP
Every diagnostic for the files under
.BR /usr/glenda/src :
.IP
.EX
lsp diags /usr/glenda/src
.EE
.SH SOURCE
plan9web's
.B rc/bin/lsp
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR acme (1),
.IR Search (1),
.IR lspfs (4)
